}

ArrayList is a class that has a Count property and implement methods IndexOf, LastIndexOf and Contains. PUT_AddContract checks the contract of Add method of ArrayList. 

In the above code, I use NUnit.Framework for writing tests and Microsoft Pex for exploring test cases.

The test coverage would be as follows:

* It checks if Count property of ArrayList is incremented when a new item is added.
* It checks if the index of the added item in the ArrayList is not less than the previous count value. This means that the new item is added at the end of the ArrayList.
* It checks if the LastIndexOf of the added item is not less than the previous count value. This means that only one instance of the new item appears in the ArrayList.
* It checks if Contains method of ArrayList returns true for the added value.
* In last, by comparing the last index of new added item with previous count, it validates that the item has been added at the last position.--------------------			Assert.GreaterOrEqual(New_arrListLastIndexOfX, Old_arrListCount, "ArrayList.Add assertion failed!");
